    id: 20, module: "Module 2: Networking for Security", title: "Network Security Architecture",
    type: "theory", duration: "30 min",
    content: `Network security architecture is the art of designing networks that balance functionality, performance, and security. A well-architected network makes attacks difficult, contains breaches when they occur, and makes malicious activity visible to defenders.\n\nCore Architectural Principles:\n\n1. Segmentation: Divide the network into logical zones of similar trust and function. Firewall policies enforce the boundaries between zones. An attacker who compromises one segment cannot automatically access others.\n\n2. Least Connectivity: Like least privilege for users, apply least connectivity to networks — only allow connections that are necessary for business functions. Everything else is denied by default.\n\n3. Visibility: Design the network so that all important traffic passes through monitoring points. Traffic that cannot be seen cannot be defended.\n\n4. Redundancy and Resilience: Critical paths should have failover options. Single points of failure create both availability risks and potential security gaps when failover paths bypass security controls.\n\n5. Simplicity: Complex architectures create security gaps from misconfiguration. The simpler and more consistent the design, the easier it is to secure and audit.\n\nModern Enterprise Network Architecture:\n\nPerimeter Zone (Internet-facing):\n- Edge routers (ISP connection)\n- DDoS protection (Cloudflare, Akamai)\n- Next-generation firewall (NGFW)\n\nDMZ:\n- Web servers, API gateways\n- Email gateways\n- DNS (authoritative)\n- VPN concentrators\n\nInternal Network (segmented by function):\n- Corporate LAN (employee workstations)\n- Server subnet (application servers)\n- Database subnet (isolated, minimal access)\n- Management network (access to all network devices — HIGHLY restricted)\n- IoT/OT network (isolated from corporate)\n\nCloud Integration:\nHybrid architectures connect on-premises networks to cloud VPCs (Virtual Private Clouds).\nSite-to-Site VPN or AWS Direct Connect/Azure ExpressRoute provides private connectivity.\nCloud Security Groups and NACLs (Network Access Control Lists) function like firewalls.\n\nSoftware-Defined Networking (SDN) and SASE:\nSDN decouples network control from hardware, enabling programmable, centrally managed security policies.\nSASE (Secure Access Service Edge) delivers network security as a cloud service, combining ZTNA, CASB, SWG, and FWaaS.\n\nZero Trust Network Architecture (ZTNA):\nReplaces the concept of trusted internal networks with per-request authentication and authorization regardless of location. Key components: Identity-aware proxy, micro-segmentation, continuous validation.`,
